course: dictionary
lesson: 10207
title: Tiptop: excellent, or a clever trick?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Tiptop» is an informal, old-fashioned word that means excellent, in the very best condition. A grandparent might say, «I'm feeling tiptop», or «the bike is in tiptop condition» after a new chain and new tyres. The clues are the words around it: the bike is in good shape, and the speaker sounds cheerful and well.
explain: Look at the context carefully. «Many teachers use TiPToP to know when to start a new paragraph» has capitals inside the word and talks about writing, not about feeling well. The capitals and the words «start a new paragraph» tell you this is a memory trick, not the everyday meaning of tiptop.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it in. «The bike is in excellent condition» still makes sense in place of «tiptop condition», so excellent is the right meaning. If the new sentence does not make sense, your meaning is wrong.
fact: «Tiptop» means excellent, in the very best condition.
fact: «Tiptop» is informal and old-fashioned, so you will hear it more from grandparents and in older stories than in everyday school writing.
fact: Phrases you may meet are «tiptop condition», «tiptop shape» and «feeling tiptop».
fact: Rarely, tiptop is a noun meaning the very top or highest point, as in «the tiptop of the hill».
fact: In New Zealand, Tip Top is a famous brand of ice cream. It is a name, so it starts with a capital letter.
exercise: Grandad says, «I'm feeling tiptop after my swim.» What does tiptop mean here? | Tired and sleepy | Cold and wet | Very ill | *Excellent, in the very best condition
exercise: «Many teachers use TiPToP to know when to start a new paragraph.» What does TiPToP help a writer remember? | How to spell tiptop | When to eat lunch | *When to start a new paragraph | Which ice cream to buy
exercise: «The runner was in tiptop shape for the race.» What does tiptop shape suggest about the runner? | Late for the race | Injured on the track | *Fit and in great condition | Lost and tired
test: «The bike is in tiptop condition.» Which word is closest in meaning to tiptop? | *Excellent | Broken | Noisy | Dull
test: Tiptop can also be a noun. What does «the tiptop of the hill» mean? | The path up the hill | A cold drink | The bottom of the valley | *The very top, the highest point
exam: Which sentence uses tiptop to mean excellent? | *«She is feeling tiptop after her holiday.» | «The tiptop of the stairs is dusty.» | «Write a new paragraph when the time changes.» | «Many teachers use TiPToP to remember paragraphs.»
